<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">Notes :      1.The above standalone results are prepared in compliance with Indian Accounting Standards ( Ind-AS ) notified by the Ministry of Corporate Affairs.      2.The Company operates only in one segment, namely   Cosmetics, Toiletries and Other Personal Care products  and there are no reportable segments in accordance with Ind-AS 108 on  Operating Segments .      3.Figures have been regrouped/rearranged wherever necessary.      4.The figures for last quarter are the balancing figure between audited figures in respect of full financial year and published year to date figures upto third quarter of the respective financial year.      5.Pursuant to equity shares buyback approved by Board of Directors of the Company on December 9, 2022, till the reporting date, the Company bought back 48,98,106 equity shares representing 3.32% of pre buyback paid up capital. The buyback resulted into total cash outflow of Rs 8,063.76 lakhs (excluding transaction cost and tax on buyback). Out of total equity shares bought back, 42,10,512 equity shares have been extinguished till the reporting date and balance on April 12th, 2023. The effect of subsequent extinguishment being adjusting event under Ind AS 10 on Events after the Reporting Period, has been duly recognised as on March 31st, 2023 itself. The Company funded the buyback from its securities premium account. Capital redemption reserve of Rs 48.98 lakhs representing the face value of equity shares bought back and extinguished has been created by transfer from general reserves of the Company.      The Company concluded the buyback on April 13th, 2023. Upto this date, the Company has bought back 49,14,159 equity shares representing 3.33% of pre buyback paid up capital and 99.99% of the Maximum buyback size. All equity shares bought back after the reporting date have been extinguished.      6.For Financial year 2023, the Board of Directors has recommended a final dividend of Rs 5/- per equity share. The final dividend is subject to the approval of shareholders in ensuing Annual General Meeting of the Company and therefore has not been recognised as a liability as at the reporting date in line with Ind AS 10 on Events after the Reporting Period.  For Financial year 2022, the Company declared a final dividend of Rs 4/- per equity share and one interim dividend of Rs 4/- per equity share. Total dividend for financial year 2022, aggregated to Rs 8/- per equity share.      7.The above standalone results have been reviewed by the Audit Committee and approved by the Board of Directors at their respective meetings held on May 03, 2023. The statutory auditors have issued an unmodified report on the above results.                                                                                                                            For and on behalf of Board of Directors                                                                                                                               Jaideep Nandi   Place : Mumbai                                                                                            Managing Director   Date  : May 03, 2023                                                                                 (DIN 06938480 )</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
